  "summary": "For a prepared high-school/basic-college beginner, this path forms a coherent bridge from a small integrated model to evidence-backed operations. Chapter19 carries one explicitly bounded small world through data families, actual parent checkpoints, modalities, tool execution, evaluation, compression and delivery. A then isolates external context and evidence; B makes request, validation, execution, return, stopping and action choice separate; C distinguishes steps, candidate coverage, selection, budgets and feedback updates. The complete training guide returns these ideas to named data/model files and specific CPU/GPU recipes without turning all experiments into one model lineage. The boundary to20 explicitly changes to an existing image-text base and separate ASR; small-world MoE and pure-tone results do not become natural-assistant capability claims. No unresolved blocking continuity issue remains in the current reviewed sources.",
